// TX FIR coefficients: 4 profiles x 128 taps (16-bit signed), AD9361 TX half-band FIR
// Layout: index = {mode[1:0], tap[6:0]} = mode*128 + tap
// The 128-tap TX FIR is a fixed half-band interpolator at 30.72 MSPS: its taps are
// bandwidth-independent, so all 4 modes store the same coefficients (verified against
// the Filter Wizard outputs for Real BW 2.6/0.75/1.3 MHz).  The per-mode passband is
// set instead by the analog BBF divider + secondary filter (see tx_filt_params in
// ad9361_spi_ctrl.v).  The 4-way duplication below keeps the ROM indexed by mode.
//   mode 0 (idx   0..127): PCM-FM  wide, Real BW 2.6 MHz (RF 5.2)
//   mode 1 (idx 128..255): SOQPSK   narrow, Real BW 0.75 MHz (RF 1.5)
//   mode 2 (idx 256..383): BPSK     mid, Real BW 1.3 MHz (RF 2.6)
//   mode 3 (idx 384..511): QPSK     mid, Real BW 1.3 MHz (RF 2.6)
// --- mode 0 ---
